WEBVTT

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.400
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:15.480
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:15.480
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.620
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.620
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.790
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.790
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.960
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.960
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.720
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.720
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.250
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.250
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.070
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:48.180
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:53.400
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:53.400
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.880
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.440
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:06.220
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:06.220
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:11.360
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:11.360
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.400
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.400
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.960
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.590
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.960
The Black Gundam

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.000
Lieutenant Apolly. How are you doing?

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.630
<i>The cockpit's different, but in three days</i>
<i>it'll be just like a part of my body.</i>

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.930
<i>We never had training according to the</i>
<i>useless instruction manuals...</i>

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.160
<i>...but we survived the "One-Year War"</i>
<i>just the same!</i>

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.540
Lieutenant Roberto.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.700
That overconfidence
could prove costly some day.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.740
<i>Yes, Lieutenant Quattro, sir!</i>

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.620
- Wow!
- You're something!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.360
He could be better than
even the captain!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.660
- We wish we were as good as you!
- Sub-Captain! One more time, please!

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.200
I'll be off sick!

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.670
Who's asking?

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:52.960
Yes! I am!

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.130
Goodbye!

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.970
Hey! Wait!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.640
All right. Bye.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.810
<i>Captain...!</i>

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.040
Skipping practice?

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.680
I'm not feeling well!

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.460
I'll be right back!

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.490
Hey!

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.390
He doesn't look sick to me.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:25.870
Kamille!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.910
Kamille!

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.770
Kamille!

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.240
What's the matter?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.870
I'm skipping practice!

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.040
<i>Kamille...!</i>

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.370
Stop it!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.510
Everyone will find out
that I'm Kamille!

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.810
Everyone already knows!

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.410
You're the only one who refuses
to acknowledge it!

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.610
- To the spaceport again?!
- What's wrong with that?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.950
Everything! You're skipping practice!

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.470
<i>Thank you for choosing</i>
<i>our linear car service today.</i>

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.700
<i>We will be leaving in thirty seconds.</i>

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.540
To the spaceport! Hurry!

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.010
It's leaving in only thirty seconds.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:44.970
That's a bad habit.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.280
You should stop it.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:51.150
<i>We will omit the countdown</i>
<i>and leave now.</i>

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.230
<i>What...?</i>

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.870
This feeling.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.470
Is it Amuro Ray?

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.080
Or could it be Lalah Sune?

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:10.730
Kamille!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.230
<i>Please be careful.</i>

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.970
<i>It's a Zero-G zone.</i>
<i>Please use the gravity boots.</i>

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.500
I know that!

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.020
I knew I'd be too late.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.750
Why the hurry?!

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.820
It's a direct flight from Earth.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.620
It's just a common spaceship.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.760
The Temptation is
Captain Bright's vessel.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:44.600
- Do you know him?
- I've received his autograph before.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.630
But he's not a Newtype, is he?

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:52.560
He was the captain of the White Base,
so I'm sure he is.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.540
I wonder about that.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:55.610
Kamille!

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:57.900
Kamille!

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:04.910
Titans.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.620
I'm glad you've returned much
more worthy of being a Titan.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:08.860
Kamille!

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.290
Kamille! You'll never see him.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:15.960
That's a girl's name, but...

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.730
...surprise, he's a boy.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:26.670
<i>...surprise, he's a boy.</i>

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.350
What's wrong? Kamille!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.480
Kamille!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.790
Are they your acquaintances,
Lieutenant Kacricon?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.050
Kamille! No! Don't go there!

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.260
Don't make fun of me!

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.560
Eat this!

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.560
Stop it!

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.460
Are you picking a fight,
knowing we're members of the Titans?!

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:01.240
What's wrong with Kamille
being a guy's name?!

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:02.970
I'm a man!

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.070
Damn you!

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:07.580
You guys!

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.690
- Take this!
- You're toast!

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.490
Kamille!

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.220
This area's off-limits to civilians!

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.830
You shouldn't say those things
about my name!

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.630
Kamille, right?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.670
What did I say that I shouldn't have?

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.770
What's the idea of speaking down to a
guy and saying 'surprise'?

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.440
I see. So that's what this is all about.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.380
Okay, I'll treat you like a guy,
if that's what you want.

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:37.970
Stop it!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:53.960
They say this colony was built
from Zeon scraps...

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.830
...but I heard it's a Titan secret base.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.670
I'm getting no response.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.770
Well, that is common
when it's peace time.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.280
I'll give it a try.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:06.830
Make sure someone finds you
before you run out of oxygen.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.080
Hey, the air lock in twenty-three opened.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.120
Is somebody leaving?

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.650
The Colony Public Corporation has some
youngsters training there.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.390
In Green Noa 2?

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.050
Call it "Gryps," or the Captain'll get mad.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.100
What a show off!

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:17.340
It's not necessarily going to
work the fourth time.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.480
It stinks... What's going on?

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.540
What's that?

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.790
A mobile suit... and a dock?

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.490
It's time I got going.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.170
There's no way you can hit a target
as small as me!

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.590
He's using a Vulcan inside his own colony?!

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:52.960
Is he insane?!

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:10.980
Don't let him get away!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.060
Guess that's good enough.

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:48.550
I'll deal with this wound later.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:01.490
I guess the Titans are still
building their organization.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.220
Set!

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:27.880
Now, let's see about this
so-called new Gundam.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:41.770
It's the Gundam!

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:43.570
<i>Did you find it?</i>

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:46.000
I found a new Gundam
on a training flight.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.070
So it's true, what we heard about
the development of Mk. II.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.570
<i>Contact the Lieutenant.</i>

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:51.410
Right!

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.920
You don't know of the A.E.U.G?!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.390
How could a high school student
not know of the A.E.U.G?!

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:22.110
You're the champion of the
Homo Avis Tournament...

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.610
...for two straight years.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:27.780
And you also won this year's
Junior Mobile Suit Tournament.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:29.950
That's impressive.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.860
Your marks are good enough
to consider you for military service.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.820
If you have nothing to do with the A.E.U.G....

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:42.820
...then why would you want to
pick a fight with a member of Titans?!

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:44.800
Huh?! Don't you find that odd?!

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:49.200
The idea that the A.E.U.G.
is a movement pursuing...

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.970
...independent self-governance rights for
people living in outer space is all a lie!

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:56.670
They're a worthless group
acting like Zeon...

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.710
...and criticizing the people on Earth.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:04.190
Gimme a break.

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:09.890
Just sit there and continue your
obstinacy forever, if you wish.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.850
I'm imagining it.

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:46.830
I must be tired.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.530
You're free to go, Mr. Kamille Bidan.

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:05.610
Kamille. A sportsman must act
with more vigor.

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:08.410
If you can't raise your voice,
you won't be winning many matches.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.540
Now, give me your hands.

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:12.960
If you were a Spacenoid
with no identification...

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:15.510
...he'd be holding you
for four or five days.

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.060
Is that so?

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.230
What is a Spacenoid?

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.830
So now you decide to talk
as soon as you're released.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.260
How convenient.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.760
I was intimidated by that blusterous person.

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:26.370
Damn you!

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:27.530
Matosh!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.410
You'll be arrested for interfering
with a government official!

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.710
He started it!

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:36.750
Kamille!

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.180
I thought I was doing you a favor
because your mother's here to pick you up.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.250
L-Let go of me!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.580
You're staying here!

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.100
What happened?!

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:12.710
Control room!

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:13.750
What's going on there?!

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.010
I can see a Mk. II!

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.820
- What's happening!
- Anyone hurt?!

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.290
Send us a relief squad, too!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:24.880
- Hey!
- Move quickly!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.660
Now hurry up! Here!

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:28.920
- What's going on?!
- What happened?!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.760
I heard a Gundam Mk. II crashed!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:32.660
Which one, unit 3 or 2?

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:33.630
What a disaster!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:34.860
Lieutenant! Damage report!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.100
A mobile suit? Why?

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.230
Get a stretcher here! I don't care which one!

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:41.240
Kamille! Where is Kamille?!

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:45.550
Kamille!

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:51.410
Wait!

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.450
Kamille!

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.620
Kamille!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.290
I hear it's Lieutenant Jerid!

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:58.420
He's completely overdoing it!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:19.910
Kamille!

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:35.320
A written apology may not be enough.

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:37.830
I'm told that there's been an accident
at the headquarters building.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:44.670
What's that?

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:52.110
S-Stop!

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:06.060
<i>Remain seated there</i>
<i>until I make a complete getaway!</i>

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.920
What in the world am I gonna do...

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.130
...after doing something like this?

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:07.380
Hmm. Let's get the Argama's help.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:08.420
<i>Roger.</i>

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:49.500
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:55.920
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:55.920
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:55.970 --> 00:23:01.300
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:55.970 --> 00:23:01.300
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:11.690
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:11.690
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:17.320
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:17.320
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:23.410
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:23.410
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:28.580
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:28.580
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:31.920
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:31.920
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:38.930
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:38.930
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.670 --> 00:23:48.400
Kamille Bidan takes on a Black Gundam.

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:51.630
With this move he bids farewell
to Green Oasis.

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:55.270
He then finds himself being chased
by another Gundam Mk. II.

00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:59.040
The extraordinary sight of two Gundams
fighting each other...

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:01.580
...signifies the dawn of a new era.

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:06.780
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Departure".

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:12.360
Next Episode

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:12.360
Departure

00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:10.160
You will see the tears of time.
